      "title": "1951 Boy Scouts Learn International Morse Code Raybrun RCA 2x 10in 78 RPM Set",
      "description": "<div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.5;color:#222;max-width:760px;\"><h2 style=\"font-size:22px;line-height:1.3;margin:0 0 12px;\">Boy Scouts International Morse Code Record Set</h2><p>Drop the needle on 1951 and hear how Boy Scouts learned their dots and dashes, one mystery signal at a time. Learn the International Morse Code is a Boy Scouts of America training album that uses the Raybrun Code-Voice Method: hear the signal, guess its meaning, then listen for the answer.</p><h3 style=\"font-size:18px;margin:20px 0 8px;\">Condition</h3><p>The original gatefold shows edge and corner wear, creases, staining and a handwritten price. Both discs show visible dust and surface marks. Playback is unverified.</p><h3 style=\"font-size:18px;margin:20px 0 8px;\">Details</h3><p>The Boy Scouts of America National Supply Service Division issued this training album. The printed guide is copyrighted 1951 by the Raybrun Company. RCA Victor pressed the two 10-inch, 78 RPM records. Set measures 12 \u00d7 10\u00bd \u00d7 \u00bd in.</p><h3 style=\"font-size:18px;margin:20px 0 8px;\">Matrix numbers</h3><p>Record 1, side 1: E1-KB-1893. Side 2: E1-KB-1894. Record 2, side 1: E1-KB-1895. Side 2: E1-KB-1896.</p><h3 style=\"font-size:18px;margin:20px 0 8px;\">Included</h3><p>Both records and the original illustrated gatefold with instructions printed inside. No practice key or buzzer included.</p><h3 style=\"font-size:18px;margin:20px 0 8px;\">Packing &amp; Shipping</h3><p>The records will be sleeved and protected with rigid pads in a corrugated box. Buyer-paid calculated shipping. Returns accepted within 30 days with buyer-paid return shipping.</p></div>",
